{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "All 12 required pairs are retained. NOT_APPLICABLE concerns only the exact gift questions; it does not reject the supported duties or authorize their removal from a broader compliance model.",
    "The authority disagreement concerns the assessment boundary. For these narrow claims expressly stated in the circular, no additional external dependency is needed, so NONE_DECLARED is used. If independent verification of the underlying legal regime is required, the external authorities are missing. Neither interpretation makes them AVAILABLE.",
    "Missing external texts include Handbook Overarching Principles section 6.4; Code of Conduct paragraphs 2.3 and 3.11; question 1 of the SFC Code of Conduct FAQs issued on 30 September 2010; and the Advertising Guidelines Applicable to Collective Investment Schemes Authorized under the Product Codes with applicable FAQ and guidance supplements. No dependency IDs are supplied. These absences limit broader interpretation and verification, rather than defeating the circular's express statements.",
    "The disclosure claim's missing-footnote annotation is stale: footnote 1 is supplied in db43e253bea18.u27.7511. The source also requires disclosure that investors may not recover principal; the claim extracts only the absence-of-guarantees limb.",
    "The advertising claim is confined to the referenced services. The full passage also prohibits deposit parallels, deposit-like implications and comparisons with bank deposit rates. These additional duties are not gift-classification predicates.",
    "Scope placement changes answers. node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e places offering in scope; node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f places linked offering in scope; the offer-level candidates place promotion in scope. A failed scope condition produces OUT_OF_SCOPE rather than the typed negative answer. Unknown scope can also prevent a result that an ordinary conjunction would resolve. Whether these are applicability boundaries or substantive elements remains unresolved.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional link with an existential non-discount gift component without expressly requiring the same component to carry that link. Mixed offers could therefore yield unsupported prohibitions unless the supplied classification establishes the component-level connection.",
    "The offer-level requirement for a 'separately identifiable' component must not exempt bundled or poorly itemised gifts. The source restricts 'any gifts'.",
    "The source regulates distributors who offer gifts. node.142f34016b300f5c110eb249 must not interpret 'provider' as merely a funder or fulfiller. node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b expressly distinguishes those roles, but the source does not resolve every third-party or agency attribution question.",
    "The source says returns or incentives 'may be considered a gift'; automatic gift classification would add an unsupported restriction. A separate discount likewise cannot exempt another gift component. A non-discount benefit still requires gift classification and the relevant offering and promotional relationship.",
    "Fund-specific scope is supported by the circular's setting, while the quoted paragraph 3.11 uses 'investment product'. The narrower candidates should not be treated as complete implementations for all investment products without resolving that distinction.",
    "TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT concerns the selected gift control only. A negative prohibition result or OUT_OF_SCOPE does not establish general permission: disclosure, advertising and section 103 requirements remain separate.",
    "The packet supplies no concrete operative interval and no executed implementation. These assessments address the supplied expressions, not verified runtime behavior or current-law applicability."
  ],
